        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Carex peregrina is a species of sedge (family Cyperaceae), with a remarkably disjunct distribution; it is found in the Azores and Madeira islands in the eastern Atlantic, and more than {{cvt|6000|km|mi}} away in the mountains of Ethiopia, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania, in east Africa. It prefers to grow in montane forests but occasionally is found sunny grasslands from {{cvt|2300|to|3500|m}} above sea level."
          }
        ]
